# Project Architecture Requirements

## 1. General Principles
- Follow DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principles
- Write clean, modular code
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Keep functions small and focused
- Implement proper error handling
- Use async/await for asynchronous operations
- Maintain consistent naming conventions
- Regularly refactor for improved maintainability

## 2. Backend Structure
- Routes have their individual file specific to the controllers they are using and then are registered in app in the routes/index.ts
- Implement three-layer architecture:
src/
├── controllers/    # Request/response handling
├── models/        # Database schemas
├── services/      # Business logic
├── routes/        # API endpoints
└── utils/         # Shared helpers
Copy- Key principles:
- Database Models are created using the custom class i created in api/utils/amptModel/index.js
- Controllers handle only request/response logic
- Services contain all business logic
- Maintain clear separation of concerns
- Group related functionality into modules

## 3. Frontend Structure (Vue 3)
- Use feature-based architecture:
src/
├── features/      # Domain-specific code
└── shared/        # Reusable code
├── components/
├── composables/
└── utils/
Copy- Key principles:
- Use Composition API for components
- Abstract common logic into reusable utilities
- Group related functionality by feature domain
- Use lucide-vue-next icons where appropriate, but avoid overuse

## 4. API Architecture
- Follow three-layer pattern:
- Web Layer (Controllers)
- Service Layer (Business Logic)
- Data Layer (Database Operations)
- Centralize all business logic in services layer